# Strings that must never appear in the public snapshot. tools/sync-public.ps1 runs
# `git grep -F -f` against the snapshot tree and refuses to push on any hit.
# Fixed strings only (no regex) - that is what -F buys us: no escaping surprises.
# This file itself is skipped by the scan (it necessarily contains the words it forbids).
# Not guarded on purpose: "投递" - in this codebase it means posting key events to a window
# (HotkeyAdapter / KeySpec), and the first dry run proved that by refusing a legitimate file.
